{% comment %}
Related Transitions Section
Shows the three transitions as a connected journey
{% endcomment %}

<section class="related-transitions">
  <div class="related-transitions__container">
    
    <h2 class="related-transitions__title">The Complete Journey</h2>
    <p class="related-transitions__subtitle">
      These three transitions form a continuous cycle. Master one, and you understand the architecture of all three.
    </p>

    <div class="related-transitions__flow">
      
      <div class="related-transitions__card related-transitions__card--sleep">
        <div class="related-transitions__card-content">
          <h3 class="related-transitions__card-title">
            <a href="/pages/sleep-to-wakefulness">Sleep → Wakefulness</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="related-transitions__card-description">
            The morning transition. Waking up fully, engaging your executive function, activating your nervous system.
          </p>
          <div class="related-transitions__card-meta">
            <span class="related-transitions__stat">
              <strong>30</strong> Articles
            </span>
            <span class="related-transitions__stat">
              <strong>3</strong> Findings
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/pages/sleep-to-wakefulness" class="related-transitions__card-arrow">
          Explore →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="related-transitions__connector">
        <svg width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none">
          <path d="M10 20L30 20M25 15L30 20L25 25" stroke="#1a1a18" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="related-transitions__card related-transitions__card--work">
        <div class="related-transitions__card-content">
          <h3 class="related-transitions__card-title">
            <a href="/pages/work-to-recovery">Work → Recovery</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="related-transitions__card-description">
            The evening transition. Moving from sustained effort toward a lower-demand part of the day.
          </p>
          <div class="related-transitions__card-meta">
            <span class="related-transitions__stat">
              <strong>28</strong> Articles
            </span>
            <span class="related-transitions__stat">
              <strong>2</strong> Findings
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/pages/work-to-recovery" class="related-transitions__card-arrow">
          Explore →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="related-transitions__connector">
        <svg width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none">
          <path d="M10 20L30 20M25 15L30 20L25 25" stroke="#1a1a18" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="related-transitions__card related-transitions__card--stimulation">
        <div class="related-transitions__card-content">
          <h3 class="related-transitions__card-title">
            <a href="/pages/stimulation-to-restoration">Stimulation → Restoration</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="related-transitions__card-description">
            The micro-transition. Resetting your nervous system during the day, managing stimulation load, restoring focus.
          </p>
          <div class="related-transitions__card-meta">
            <span class="related-transitions__stat">
              <strong>25</strong> Articles
            </span>
            <span class="related-transitions__stat">
              <strong>2</strong> Findings
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/pages/stimulation-to-restoration" class="related-transitions__card-arrow">
          Explore →
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="related-transitions__insight">
      <p>
        These territories may involve different practical cues, contexts and constraints. <strong>Mirellis does not claim that one mechanism explains every transition.</strong> Each public record keeps its evidence basis and limits visible.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .related-transitions {
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .related-transitions__container {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .related-transitions__title {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: #1a1a18;
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .related-transitions__subtitle {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #666;
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem auto;
  }

  .related-transitions__flow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .related-transitions__card {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 250px;
    max-width: 300px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #faf7f2;
    border-radius: 4px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .related-transitions__card:hover {
    background: #f5f2ed;
  }

  .related-transitions__card-content {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .related-transitions__card-title {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .related-transitions__card-title a {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #1a1a18;
    text-decoration: none;
    line-height: 1.4;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .related-transitions__card-title a:hover {
    color: #666;
  }

  .related-transitions__card-description {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #666;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .related-transitions__card-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #999;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .related-transitions__stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .related-transitions__stat strong {
    color: #1a1a18;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    display: block;
  }

  .related-transitions__card-arrow {
    align-self: flex-start;
    color: #1a1a18;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .related-transitions__card-arrow:hover {
    color: #666;
  }

  .related-transitions__connector {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .related-transitions__connector svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .related-transitions__insight {
    padding: 2rem;
    background: #faf7f2;
    border-radius: 4px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .related-transitions__insight p {
    font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #1a1a18;
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .related-transitions__flow {
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .related-transitions__card {
      min-width: 220px;
      max-width: 260px;
      padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .related-transitions__card-title a {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .related-transitions {
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem;
    }

    .related-transitions__title {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .related-transitions__subtitle {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .related-transitions__flow {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .related-transitions__connector {
      width: 30px;
      height: 30px;
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }

    .related-transitions__card {
      max-width: 100%;
    }

    .related-transitions__card-meta {
      justify-content: space-around;
    }

    .related-transitions__insight {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }

    .related-transitions__insight p {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }
  }
</style>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Related Transitions",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
